  "articleBody": "There are a lot of ideas floating around about non-slip kitchen flooring, so let's clear up some common myths with solid facts. Myth: All textured floors are equally slip-resistant. Fact: Not true! While texture can help, true slip resistance is a measured factor, and some textured surfaces can still be slippery when wet. Always look for specific ratings. Myth: Cleaning products don't affect a floor's slip resistance. Fact: They absolutely can. Some cleaning products leave residues that actually reduce traction, making your floor less safe. Myth: Any floor that looks good will be safe. Fact: Appearance can be deceiving. A floor might look fantastic, but if it doesn't offer proper slip resistance, especially in wet kitchen zones, it's not truly safe. Myth: Slip resistance only matters in commercial kitchens. Fact: Slips and falls happen in homes too! Kitchens are high-spill zones, so good slip resistance is important for everyone, especially those with mobility challenges. When in doubt, or if you have specific accessibility needs, it's a good idea to chat with a remodeling expert who understands both product specifics and proper installation.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
